.TH DIGICARLO-GUI 1 "2026-09-24" "DigiCarlo 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
digicarlo-gui \- the DigiCarlo window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B digicarlo-gui
.RB [ \-\-classic ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The window does what \fBdigicarlo\fR(1) does, as a Windows 95 program looking
into a garage pre-rendered the way a 1995 CD-ROM game was, with a console of
Nash Metropolitan hardware along the bottom.
.SS The garage
Click the card in the reader, or the camera on the bench, to pull its new
pictures into the archive; the card's tag says how many are new. The Photo
Board is where the waiting shots are dated. The darkroom door, like
\fBSTART\fR, puts them in the library. The crate of originals opens the
archive folder, and the car honks and looks for cameras again. The calendar
shows today, the date a pull's newest shot gets, and the safelight is on
while shots are waiting.
.PP
The radio's keys in the garage:
.TP
.B CHECK CARD
Read every file on the card to its end, and look in the kernel's log for
read errors.
.TP
.B EJECT
Unmount the card and power off the reader, so it can be pulled out.
.TP
.B ERASE CARD
Empty the card for next time: only when every file on it has a copy in the
archive, compared byte for byte, and otherwise nothing.
.TP
.B SYNC
Ask Syncthing whether the phone is connected, and how much of the library
it has.
.TP
.B LIBRARY
Open the library folder.
.SS The Photo Board
Every waiting shot is pinned up as a print, each session led by an index
card with what the camera's clock said and the dates its shots will get.
Click a print to pick it (Shift for a run, Ctrl for one more), or a card
for its whole session. On the ledge: the date stamp starts the picked shots
at a date you give; the alarm clock keeps the camera's own dates; the eraser
goes back to automatic; the wastebasket leaves them out (with nothing
picked, it brings back the ones left out); the red-eye pen takes the flash
red out of their eyes. The radio's keys there are \fBVIEW\fR, \fBROTATE\fR,
\fBNAME\fR, \fBPLACE\fR and \fBUNDO\fR; its knobs, the mouse wheel and Page
Up/Down turn the pages.
.PP
Rotation, names, places and red-eye fixes go into the library copies as
they are made; the archive copy never changes. What is decided is kept in
\fI~/.config/digicarlo/board.json\fR until the shots are developed.
.PP
After a pull from a camera whose clock can be right (the Polaroid i1237 and
Konica KD-400Z to begin with; see \fBtrust_clock_cameras\fR), a dialog asks
which of its sessions to date by the camera.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-classic
The window of DigiCarlo 1.1 and 1.2 instead.
.SH NOTES
It needs PyQt6 (\fBpython3-pyqt6\fR). The green screen looks as intended with
\fBfonts-glasstty\fR, the handwriting with \fBfonts-comic-neue\fR, and the
printing with \fBfonts-nunito\fR. The red-eye pen needs \fBpython3-numpy\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR digicarlo (1)
